  "description": "The Foundation RULE value contract as republished in OBDS 3.0.0. Two corrections, both of which the compiler now enforces and which the 1.0.0 contract could not state. First, RULE-level validatorRef is removed: Foundation Validator Registry v1 is closed, has one entry, and that entry applies to value contracts of kind colour with the element value as its input, so the set of rule-level references that could resolve was empty and the deterministic-plus-empty-checks branch was unsatisfiable by construction. Second, checks was an untyped array, so an authoring document could declare a check no registry primitive recognises and only the compiler would notice. A deterministic RULE now declares at least one registered Foundation check, in the schema as well as in the compiler.",
